1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:02,733
SAT function questions
come in four disguises:

2
00:00:02,753 --> 00:00:06,147
an equation, a graph, a
table, or a word problem.

3
00:00:06,397 --> 00:00:08,984
Underneath, they all ask
about the same thing:

4
00:00:09,004 --> 00:00:10,753
inputs and outputs.

5
00:00:10,804 --> 00:00:14,784
In this lesson: function notation,
reading graphs and tables,

6
00:00:14,804 --> 00:00:19,642
shifting and flipping graphs, and
what the numbers mean in context.

7
00:00:19,662 --> 00:00:23,340
Then six practice questions,
from easy to hard.

8
00:00:23,412 --> 00:00:26,213
One mistake to fix right away.

9
00:00:26,233 --> 00:00:32,071
A lot of students think f of the quantity
x minus two moves a graph two units

10
00:00:32,091 --> 00:00:33,035
left.

11
00:00:33,055 --> 00:00:35,879
It actually moves it
right, and you'll see why.

12
00:00:35,899 --> 00:00:40,935
A function is a rule that turns
each input into exactly one output.

13
00:00:40,970 --> 00:00:44,255
f of x is the output when the input is x.

14
00:00:44,334 --> 00:00:48,742
Here's our home graph: y equals f of x,

15
00:00:48,762 --> 00:00:50,619
a parabola that opens down.

16
00:00:51,119 --> 00:00:54,599
To find f of two, go to two on the x axis,

17
00:00:54,619 --> 00:00:57,064
move up to the curve, and read the height.

18
00:00:57,084 --> 00:00:58,227
It's three.

19
00:00:58,262 --> 00:01:00,584
So f of two equals three.

20
00:01:00,613 --> 00:01:01,700
Now flip the question.

21
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:05,235
If f of x equals three, which inputs work?

22
00:01:05,255 --> 00:01:07,770
That's a horizontal line at height three.

23
00:01:07,790 --> 00:01:12,370
It hits the curve twice, at x
equals zero and x equals two.

24
00:01:12,390 --> 00:01:14,119
With an equation, same idea.

25
00:01:14,139 --> 00:01:19,547
If f of x is x squared minus two
x, and f of a equals twenty-four,

26
00:01:19,567 --> 00:01:23,032
solve a squared minus
two a equals twenty-four.

27
00:01:23,103 --> 00:01:26,527
It factors, and a is six or negative four.

28
00:01:26,547 --> 00:01:29,777
A table is just a list
of input output pairs,

29
00:01:29,797 --> 00:01:32,884
so f of three is whatever
sits under three.

30
00:01:32,904 --> 00:01:36,955
And f of g of x means:
run x through g first,

31
00:01:36,975 --> 00:01:39,724
then feed that answer into f.

32
00:01:39,832 --> 00:01:40,863
Inside out.

33
00:01:40,883 --> 00:01:43,184
Next, the features of a graph.

34
00:01:43,204 --> 00:01:45,970
The y intercept is where x equals zero,

35
00:01:45,990 --> 00:01:47,506
so it's f of zero.

36
00:01:47,526 --> 00:01:50,370
On our graph, that's zero, three.

37
00:01:50,390 --> 00:01:52,940
The x intercepts are
where the height is zero,

38
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:55,405
so they solve f of x equals zero.

39
00:01:55,425 --> 00:01:57,583
Here, negative one and three.

40
00:01:57,603 --> 00:01:59,941
They're also called the zeros of f.

41
00:01:59,961 --> 00:02:04,993
So f of zero is a height, but f of
x equals zero gives you x values.

42
00:02:05,013 --> 00:02:07,028
The maximum is the highest point: here,

43
00:02:07,048 --> 00:02:08,279
one, four.

44
00:02:08,299 --> 00:02:10,636
The maximum value is the height, four,

45
00:02:10,656 --> 00:02:12,600
and it happens at x equals one.

46
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:15,099
The graph is increasing
for x less than one,

47
00:02:15,119 --> 00:02:16,916
and decreasing after that.

48
00:02:16,936 --> 00:02:19,523
And to count solutions to f of x equals k,

49
00:02:19,543 --> 00:02:22,222
slide a horizontal line to height k.

50
00:02:22,329 --> 00:02:24,595
At height three, two crossings.

51
00:02:24,615 --> 00:02:27,115
At four, just one, the peak.

52
00:02:27,185 --> 00:02:28,935
At five, none.

53
00:02:28,977 --> 00:02:30,513
Now transformations.

54
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:34,636
Adding outside the function
moves the graph vertically.

55
00:02:34,656 --> 00:02:39,048
f of x, plus two, lifts
every point two units.

56
00:02:39,298 --> 00:02:42,279
Our peak at one, four moves up to one,

57
00:02:42,299 --> 00:02:43,234
six.

58
00:02:43,254 --> 00:02:45,948
Changing the input moves
the graph sideways,

59
00:02:45,968 --> 00:02:47,770
and it goes the opposite
way from the sign.

60
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:53,234
f of the quantity x minus three
moves the graph three units right.

61
00:02:53,254 --> 00:02:56,948
The peak moves from one, four to four,

62
00:02:56,968 --> 00:02:57,803
four.

63
00:02:57,823 --> 00:02:58,823
Here's why.

64
00:02:59,109 --> 00:03:02,196
To reach the old peak, x
minus three has to equal one,

65
00:03:02,216 --> 00:03:03,660
so x equals four.

66
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:06,873
Every input has to be three
bigger to get the same output,

67
00:03:06,893 --> 00:03:09,072
so everything lands three units right.

68
00:03:09,104 --> 00:03:11,069
Last, a negative out front.

69
00:03:11,175 --> 00:03:14,441
Negative f of x multiplies
every output by negative one,

70
00:03:14,461 --> 00:03:16,691
so the graph flips over the x axis.

71
00:03:16,711 --> 00:03:20,226
The maximum at one, four
becomes a minimum at one,

72
00:03:20,246 --> 00:03:21,370
negative four.

73
00:03:21,390 --> 00:03:23,650
The x intercepts stay put.

74
00:03:23,670 --> 00:03:26,471
In word problems, every
number means something.

75
00:03:26,491 --> 00:03:30,293
In a quadratic height model, the
constant is the starting height,

76
00:03:30,313 --> 00:03:33,364
the vertex is the maximum
height and when it happens,

77
00:03:33,384 --> 00:03:35,991
and the positive zero is when it lands.

78
00:03:36,039 --> 00:03:40,396
In an exponential model like eight
hundred times one point oh five to the t,

79
00:03:40,468 --> 00:03:44,983
eight hundred is the starting value, and
one point oh five means growth of five

80
00:03:45,003 --> 00:03:46,753
percent per period.

81
00:03:46,818 --> 00:03:49,155
So sort each question first.

82
00:03:49,175 --> 00:03:51,139
Evaluate or solve?

83
00:03:51,318 --> 00:03:53,675
A feature of a graph or table?

84
00:03:53,711 --> 00:03:55,298
A shift or a flip?

85
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:57,691
Or what a number means in context?

86
00:03:57,711 --> 00:03:58,782
Let's practice.

87
00:03:58,842 --> 00:03:59,786
Question one.

88
00:03:59,806 --> 00:04:04,536
The functions f and g are defined by
f of x equals x squared minus two x,

89
00:04:04,556 --> 00:04:07,285
and g of x equals three x plus one.

90
00:04:07,305 --> 00:04:09,998
What is the value of g of f of four?

91
00:04:10,018 --> 00:04:11,411
Pause and try it.

92
00:04:14,636 --> 00:04:15,437
Inside out.

93
00:04:15,457 --> 00:04:18,079
f of four comes first:
sixteen minus eight,

94
00:04:18,099 --> 00:04:19,116
which is eight.

95
00:04:19,136 --> 00:04:20,330
Then that eight goes into g.

96
00:04:20,350 --> 00:04:23,686
Three times eight, plus
one, is twenty-five.

97
00:04:23,706 --> 00:04:25,493
The answer is C.

98
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:28,340
Eight is f of four: you stopped halfway.

99
00:04:28,483 --> 00:04:31,214
Thirteen is g of four, which skips f.

100
00:04:31,234 --> 00:04:33,820
And one hundred forty-three
is f of g of four:

101
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:36,046
the right functions in the wrong order.

102
00:04:36,066 --> 00:04:37,209
Question two.

103
00:04:37,494 --> 00:04:40,546
The graph of y equals f of x is shown.

104
00:04:40,566 --> 00:04:44,744
How many solutions does the
equation f of x equals three have?

105
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:46,173
Pause and try it.

106
00:04:49,398 --> 00:04:53,449
f of x equals three asks: where
is the graph's height three?

107
00:04:53,469 --> 00:04:56,842
So draw a horizontal
line at y equals three,

108
00:04:56,862 --> 00:04:58,861
and count where it meets the curve.

109
00:04:58,911 --> 00:05:01,284
The curve climbs to a peak at height four,

110
00:05:01,304 --> 00:05:04,855
falls to a low point at height
zero, then climbs again.

111
00:05:04,875 --> 00:05:06,997
A line at height three sits between those,

112
00:05:07,017 --> 00:05:08,854
so it's crossed three times.

113
00:05:08,874 --> 00:05:10,518
The answer is D.

114
00:05:10,544 --> 00:05:11,953
The trap is B.

115
00:05:11,973 --> 00:05:16,774
It treats three as an x value, as if
the only solution were x equals three.

116
00:05:16,794 --> 00:05:18,738
That's reading the wrong axis.

117
00:05:18,758 --> 00:05:23,060
f of x is the output, so f of x
equals three is a horizontal line.

118
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:25,703
And two is the number of x intercepts,

119
00:05:25,723 --> 00:05:28,177
which answers f of x equals zero.

120
00:05:28,197 --> 00:05:29,248
Question three.

121
00:05:29,268 --> 00:05:35,141
The function h is defined by h of t equals
negative five t squared plus twenty t

122
00:05:35,161 --> 00:05:36,340
plus twenty-five.

123
00:05:36,482 --> 00:05:41,070
It gives the height, in meters, of a ball
above the ground t seconds after it is

124
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:42,518
launched from a platform.

125
00:05:42,563 --> 00:05:46,793
According to the model, how many seconds
after it is launched does the ball hit

126
00:05:46,813 --> 00:05:47,628
the ground?

127
00:05:47,648 --> 00:05:49,041
Pause and try it.

128
00:05:53,266 --> 00:05:55,996
Hitting the ground means
the height is zero.

129
00:05:56,016 --> 00:05:59,496
So set h of t equal to
zero, not t equal to zero.

130
00:05:59,516 --> 00:06:04,889
Divide every term by negative five: t
squared minus four t minus five equals

131
00:06:04,909 --> 00:06:05,703
zero.

132
00:06:05,723 --> 00:06:09,059
That factors into t minus
five, times t plus one.

133
00:06:09,079 --> 00:06:11,917
So t is five or negative one.

134
00:06:11,937 --> 00:06:14,094
Negative one second
isn't after the launch,

135
00:06:14,114 --> 00:06:15,826
so the answer is five.

136
00:06:15,846 --> 00:06:17,238
Now look at the traps.

137
00:06:17,346 --> 00:06:20,846
Twenty-five is h of zero,
the height of the platform.

138
00:06:20,953 --> 00:06:25,926
Two is when the ball is highest, and
forty-five meters is that maximum height.

139
00:06:25,946 --> 00:06:27,125
Question four.

140
00:06:27,161 --> 00:06:32,176
The function f is defined by f
of x equals x squared minus four.

141
00:06:32,196 --> 00:06:37,890
In the x y plane, the graph of y equals
g of x is the result of translating the

142
00:06:37,910 --> 00:06:41,569
graph of y equals f of x
three units to the right.

143
00:06:41,589 --> 00:06:43,482
Which equation defines g?

144
00:06:43,617 --> 00:06:45,010
Pause and try it.

145
00:06:48,235 --> 00:06:51,929
Right three means replacing
x with x minus three.

146
00:06:51,949 --> 00:06:56,000
So g of x equals f of the
quantity x minus three,

147
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:58,500
which is the quantity
x minus three, squared,

148
00:06:58,520 --> 00:06:59,806
minus four.

149
00:06:59,841 --> 00:07:01,570
The answer is A.

150
00:07:01,590 --> 00:07:02,463
Check with the vertex.

151
00:07:02,483 --> 00:07:05,070
f's vertex is zero, negative four.

152
00:07:05,090 --> 00:07:07,356
Choice A puts it at three, negative four:

153
00:07:07,376 --> 00:07:08,712
three to the right.

154
00:07:08,732 --> 00:07:11,142
B puts it at negative
three, which is left.

155
00:07:11,162 --> 00:07:15,661
C and D change the number outside,
so they move the graph up or down.

156
00:07:15,693 --> 00:07:18,959
Before the harder questions,
the three traps in one place.

157
00:07:18,979 --> 00:07:23,049
First, a shift inside the parentheses
goes opposite to its sign.

158
00:07:23,192 --> 00:07:25,800
Minus means right, plus means left.

159
00:07:25,825 --> 00:07:30,091
Second, f of x equals
zero is not x equals zero.

160
00:07:30,111 --> 00:07:32,376
Zeros are x intercepts.

161
00:07:32,396 --> 00:07:34,662
f of zero is the y intercept.

162
00:07:34,682 --> 00:07:38,253
Third, f of x equals k
is a horizontal line.

163
00:07:38,307 --> 00:07:40,321
Question five, a harder one.

164
00:07:40,341 --> 00:07:46,215
The table shows several values of x and
f of x for the quadratic function f.

165
00:07:46,235 --> 00:07:50,715
For x equals zero through five,
the values of f of x are two,

166
00:07:50,735 --> 00:07:53,715
negative two, negative
four, negative four,

167
00:07:53,735 --> 00:07:55,715
negative two, and two.

168
00:07:55,735 --> 00:07:58,057
What is the minimum value of f?

169
00:07:58,109 --> 00:07:59,374
Pause and try it.

170
00:07:59,394 --> 00:08:00,929
Take a little longer on this one.

171
00:08:05,149 --> 00:08:06,915
The tempting answer is negative four,

172
00:08:06,935 --> 00:08:08,807
the smallest number in the table.

173
00:08:08,827 --> 00:08:11,200
But a table only shows some inputs.

174
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:13,396
The lowest point might fall between them.

175
00:08:13,416 --> 00:08:14,952
Use symmetry.

176
00:08:15,381 --> 00:08:18,003
A parabola is symmetric about its vertex,

177
00:08:18,023 --> 00:08:21,539
and f of two and f of three
are both negative four.

178
00:08:21,559 --> 00:08:26,023
So the vertex is halfway between,
at x equals two point five.

179
00:08:26,050 --> 00:08:28,316
To get the height there,
build the equation.

180
00:08:28,336 --> 00:08:31,316
f of zero is two, so c is two.

181
00:08:31,336 --> 00:08:34,816
The next two rows give a
plus b equals negative four,

182
00:08:34,836 --> 00:08:37,851
and two a plus b equals negative three.

183
00:08:37,871 --> 00:08:41,336
Subtract: a is one, b is negative five.

184
00:08:41,363 --> 00:08:46,220
So f of x is x squared
minus five x plus two.

185
00:08:46,328 --> 00:08:49,236
Plug in two point five:
six point two five,

186
00:08:49,256 --> 00:08:52,271
minus twelve point five, plus two.

187
00:08:52,291 --> 00:08:54,665
That's negative four point two five.

188
00:08:54,685 --> 00:08:56,220
The answer is B.

189
00:08:56,263 --> 00:08:58,242
Two point five is where
the minimum happens,

190
00:08:58,262 --> 00:08:59,564
not its value.

191
00:08:59,584 --> 00:09:03,656
And negative six point two five is
what you get if you drop the plus two.

192
00:09:03,676 --> 00:09:07,299
Faster in Desmos: enter
the table, then type y one,

193
00:09:07,319 --> 00:09:10,514
tilde, a x one squared, plus b x one,

194
00:09:10,534 --> 00:09:11,534
plus c.

195
00:09:11,854 --> 00:09:15,299
Desmos reports a equals
one, b equals negative five,

196
00:09:15,319 --> 00:09:16,727
c equals two.

197
00:09:16,747 --> 00:09:18,712
Then click the bottom of the curve.

198
00:09:18,759 --> 00:09:20,473
Last one, the hardest.

199
00:09:21,009 --> 00:09:27,060
In the x y plane, the graph of y equals
f of x has its maximum at the point one,

200
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:28,080
six.

201
00:09:28,187 --> 00:09:34,168
The function g is defined by g of x
equals negative f of the quantity x minus

202
00:09:34,188 --> 00:09:34,953
two.

203
00:09:34,973 --> 00:09:38,968
Which statement about the graph
of y equals g of x must be true?

204
00:09:38,988 --> 00:09:42,576
The choices: A, a maximum at three, six.

205
00:09:42,596 --> 00:09:46,040
B, a minimum at negative
one, negative six.

206
00:09:46,060 --> 00:09:49,003
C, a minimum at three, negative six.

207
00:09:49,023 --> 00:09:51,880
D, a maximum at negative one, six.

208
00:09:51,915 --> 00:09:53,181
Pause and try it.

209
00:09:53,201 --> 00:09:54,736
Take a little longer on this one.

210
00:09:58,956 --> 00:10:00,007
We don't need the equation of f.

211
00:10:00,027 --> 00:10:04,007
Follow the one point we
know, one change at a time.

212
00:10:04,027 --> 00:10:08,578
First, the inside: x minus two
moves everything two units right.

213
00:10:08,598 --> 00:10:11,364
The peak goes from one, six to three,

214
00:10:11,384 --> 00:10:12,319
six.

215
00:10:12,339 --> 00:10:14,033
Next, the negative out front.

216
00:10:14,053 --> 00:10:16,712
It multiplies every
output by negative one,

217
00:10:16,732 --> 00:10:19,660
so the graph flips over the x axis.

218
00:10:19,695 --> 00:10:23,461
The peak at height six becomes
a low point at negative six.

219
00:10:23,481 --> 00:10:27,104
So g has a minimum at three, negative six.

220
00:10:27,124 --> 00:10:28,624
The answer is C.

221
00:10:28,666 --> 00:10:31,467
A shifted right but forgot the flip.

222
00:10:31,487 --> 00:10:34,523
B and D shifted the
wrong way, to the left.

223
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:39,540
To check in Desmos, make up
any f with a maximum at one,

224
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:43,611
six, like negative the
quantity x minus one,

225
00:10:43,631 --> 00:10:45,611
squared, plus six.

226
00:10:45,631 --> 00:10:51,290
Then type g of x equals negative
f of the quantity x minus two,

227
00:10:51,310 --> 00:10:52,632
and click the low point.

228
00:10:52,686 --> 00:10:54,079
The test-day method.

229
00:10:54,114 --> 00:10:57,416
Step one: name what they
give you, an equation,

230
00:10:57,436 --> 00:11:00,221
a graph, a table, or a context.

231
00:11:00,293 --> 00:11:02,629
Step two: translate.

232
00:11:02,649 --> 00:11:05,042
f of a means plug in.

233
00:11:05,185 --> 00:11:09,773
f of x equals k means solve,
or draw a horizontal line.

234
00:11:09,793 --> 00:11:12,411
Zeros mean f of x equals zero.

235
00:11:12,431 --> 00:11:15,839
Step three: for shifts and
flips, track one key point,

236
00:11:15,859 --> 00:11:17,947
like a vertex or an intercept.

237
00:11:17,967 --> 00:11:20,482
Inside changes go the opposite way.

238
00:11:20,502 --> 00:11:22,780
Outside changes do what they say.

239
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:26,136
Step four: use Desmos when it saves work:

240
00:11:26,156 --> 00:11:29,494
counting solutions, finding
a maximum or an intercept,

241
00:11:29,514 --> 00:11:31,637
checking a shift, or fitting a table.

242
00:11:31,657 --> 00:11:34,506
For a single substitution,
just do it by hand.

243
00:11:34,526 --> 00:11:37,613
And before you submit,
reread what they asked for.

244
00:11:37,633 --> 00:11:40,026
An x value or a y value?

245
00:11:40,133 --> 00:11:42,919
Where the minimum happens, or what it is?

246
00:11:42,966 --> 00:11:45,624
That's nonlinear functions:
inputs and outputs,

247
00:11:45,644 --> 00:11:48,803
horizontal lines for outputs,
inside shifts in reverse,

248
00:11:48,823 --> 00:11:50,910
and a negative that flips the graph.

249
00:11:50,930 --> 00:11:54,731
For more practice, the free Question
Bank lets you filter Advanced Math by

250
00:11:54,751 --> 00:11:56,251
nonlinear functions.

251
00:11:56,336 --> 00:11:59,459
Every question in this video
